./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-28ok1k/TASK-260715-28ok1k_audit-scope.md:1:Pin + audit the two SSH engine candidates for the in-extension transport. CANDIDATES: (A) SwiftNIO SSH (apple/swift-nio-ssh) as the ReluxNIOSSH fork basis — pure Swift, embeddable in the NE extension, but upstream states it is BUILDING BLOCKS not a production client and supports only modern algorithms (Ed25519/ECDSA host keys, AES-GCM, curve25519/x25519); (B) libssh2 — wider algorithm set + explicit channel-window control, C library. Per .spec/ssh-transport.md and ADR-005 (direct-tcpip for TCP + exec/stdio relay for UDP), ADR-006 (upload via exec stdin, NO SFTP), ADR-014 (engine selection is OPEN, gated on this audit + later tests), ADR-019 (ReluxNIOSSH stays a SOURCE SwiftPM dep; libssh2 packaged as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the 1g9cyt native seam). AUDIT each candidate: (1) pin exact version/commit + license (NIOSSH Apache-2.0, libssh2 BSD — confirm + notices); (2) API surface for direct-tcpip channels, exec channels, and stdin upload; (3) algorithm coverage — kex, cipher, MAC, host-key — measured against real-world OpenSSH server defaults incl. whether RSA host keys / older servers are reachable; (4) PER-CHANNEL WINDOW control (go/no-go for the memory budget — can window size be set/observed per channel?); (5) REKEY support and behavior under sustained multi-GB transfer (go/no-go — VPN traffic forces rekey; note any known failure); (6) concurrency headroom (target 500-1000 simultaneous channels) and per-channel/base memory footprint; (7) build/embedding path (NIOSSH SwiftPM source vs libssh2 XCFramework). Deliver a dated TASK-ID-scoped comparative audit usable by TASK-260715-2ny6z4 (conformance contract), nzdzv3 (NIOSSH fork), 1af33i/1ozsb6 (adapters). Do NOT select the engine here (that is TASK-260715-1gjxer, gated on functional/rekey/scale tests + physical evidence); audit both fairly. If a claim cannot be verified from source/docs, note the gap; do not guess.
