./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-3a2dnr/TASK-260728-3a2dnr_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-645ab7.log:4627:.spec/decisions.md:18:| ADR-014 | Accepted | Select **libssh2** as the primary SSH engine (2026-07-28 owner decision). `ReluxNIOSSH` is retained as recorded comparative evidence and receives no further fork work unless new evidence invalidates libssh2. Selection rests on the ADR-023 M0-viability gate set plus macOS-harness conformance evidence; per-channel window, scale, and memory numbers remain M3 physical-evidence gates and are not asserted by this decision. |
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-3a2dnr/TASK-260728-3a2dnr_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-645ab7.log:4631:.spec/decisions.md:28:| ADR-023 | Accepted | Scope the M0 SSH transport contract to **viability** (Option A). M0-viability-mandatory: pre-auth raw host-key evidence, approved public-key authentication, `direct-tcpip`, bidirectional exec plus exec/stdin relay upload, client-initiated rekey by byte/time threshold, bounded buffers and backpressure, deterministic cancellation and lifecycle, keepalive, privacy-safe errors, and cheaply-available metrics. Deferred to M3 as explicitly evidence-gated obligations, never silent waivers: (1) consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap, (2) the RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy, (3) exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing `status(0)` from `notReported` and exposing `coreDumped`, (4) deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT/timeout/miss. M0 adapters MUST surface deferred semantics as explicit not-reported/unsupported states. Owner tasks: `TASK-260728-yx2fca` (contract re-scope), `TASK-260728-3cveay` (M3 delivery). Resolves the three-round `TASK-260715-1ozsb6` stop-the-line. |
