./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:1480:scope:In scope: consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap that is not auto-adjusted before consumer delivery; RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy preserved end to end; exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing status 0 from absent metadata and exposing exit-signal coreDumped; deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT, timeout, and miss metrics; the fork or upstream change needed on the selected engine plus its maintenance and rebase owner; conformance tests and harness evidence. Out of scope: re-opening the M0 engine selection, NIOSSH fork work while libssh2 remains primary, lane scheduling policy, and hardcoding numeric window or rekey values outside the accepted memory ledger.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:1481:ac:1. Each of the four deferred semantics is implemented or explicitly recorded red with pinned-source evidence; no semantic is silently dropped. 2. Receive-window credit is consumer-driven with an immutable cap proven by a test that stalls the consumer and observes no credit return. 3. Channel-open rejection reasons, exec exit status/notReported/coreDumped, and server-rekey generation plus keepalive RTT/timeout/miss are asserted against a real SSH host, not mocks. 4. Every added buffer, window, and metric fits the accepted TASK-260715-1pn983 memory ledger and the task reports measured footprint deltas. 5. Any engine fork records exact pinned revision, patch scope, security-monitoring, and rebase owner.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:1482:preconditionResources:[{"name":"TASK-260728-3cveay_approved-m0-viability-decision.md","uri":"file://TASK-260728-3cveay/TASK-260728-3cveay_approved-m0-viability-decision.md","description":"Human-approved 2026-07-28 SSH scope and candidate decision"},{"name":"TASK-260728-3cveay_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md","uri":"file://TASK-260728-3cveay/TASK-260728-3cveay_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md","description":"Binding deferred SSH semantics and pinned evidence inherited from M0 rescope"}]
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:1488:ac:1. The M0-viability tier adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for the macOS harness and macOS provider configuration and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence before authentication, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, exec/stdin upload, client rekey, server-rekey handling, bounded buffers, keepalive, available metrics, Keychain-only secret references, and privacy-safe errors satisfy every M0-viability-mandatory row or remain red with reproducible evidence. 4. The four M3-deferred semantics are emitted as explicit not-reported or unsupported states and are traceable to TASK-260728-3cveay; no deferred value is fabricated. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.
