./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:2117:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-_RUN-260809-7d007e.log:33992:ac:1. The adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for the macOS harness and the macOS provider configuration and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence before authentication, public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, exec/stdin upload, EOF and half-close, keepalive, available metrics, and privacy-safe errors conform or are marked red with reproducible evidence. 4. Client-initiated rekey by byte and time threshold is proven through supported APIs of the accepted fork; the four M3-deferred semantics are emitted as explicit not-reported or unsupported states and are traceable to TASK-260728-3cveay. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.
