./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260809-0bc9aa.log:10761:/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260728-yx2fca, name=TASK-260728-yx2fca_results.md, type=outcome, content=\"# TASK-260728-yx2fca reviewer results\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nChanges requested. Route: to-dev.\\n\\n## Required change\\n\\nP1 — The RFC 4254 channel-open rejection semantic can still be silently absent.\\n\\nSources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift lines 1173 and 1181 declare SSHTransportError.channelOpenReason as an optional SSHDeferredSemanticReport and give it a nil default. As a result, a caller can construct code=.channelOpenRejected without reported, notReported, or unsupported. This violates acceptance criterion 3 and the canonical contract lines 17-20 and 55, which require unavailable deferred semantics to be explicit rather than silently omitted.\\n\\nTests/ReluxTunnelCoreTests/SSHTransportContractTests.swift lines 433-450 prove reported and unsupported values, but do not close or reject the nil path.\\n\\nRequired rework: make every channel-open rejection require an explicit deferred report at the neutral seam while preserving a clear not-applicable representation for non-channel-open errors. Add a focused regression test proving a channel-open rejection cannot exist with silent absence.\\n\\n## Accepted evidence\\n\\n- The contract registry classifies 16 M0-viability-mandatory requirements and exactly four M3-deferred requirements owned by TASK-260728-3cveay.\\n- The canonical contract individually names all four deferred semantics and includes pinned libssh2/ReluxNIOSSH evidence.\\n- Host-key-before-authentication, approved public-key authentication, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client rekey, bounded buffers/backpressure, deterministic cancellation/lifecycle, Keychain-only secret references, keepalive transmission, available observability, and privacy-safe errors remain mandatory.\\n- TASK-260715-1ozsb6, TASK-260715-2d3g5e, and TASK-260715-1u2vpc each carry the byte-identical revised contract and viability-tier acceptance criteria.\\n- The M3 owner TASK-260728-3cveay carries the same contract.\\n- Existing libssh2 and ReluxNIOSSH blocker/audit resources remain attached and referenced.\\n\\n## Reviewer validation\\n\\n- swift format lint --recursive --strict Sources Tests Package.swift: exit 0.\\n- git diff --check: exit 0.\\n- ./scripts/check-core-boundaries.sh: exit 0.\\n- swift test --filter SSHTransportContractTests: exit 0; 13 tests in 1 suite passed.\\n- make validate-core: exit 0; native/libssh2 verification passed, 336 tests in 29 suites passed, swift build passed.\\n- task-board validate: exit 0; reports PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH for STORY-260715-lkshfz because child aggregate reviewing is suppressed by the known unfinished hard blocker.\\n\\nReviewer made no implementation-file changes.\", description=\"Reviewer verdict and validation evidence\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel
